# Train Flat Within-Mouse Triplet 5 FPS Experiment

This workflow trains the flat Social Attention architecture on all three mice
while limiting spatial attention to keypoints from the same mouse. Cross-mouse
spatial edges are removed, but each mouse is still predicted in the shared arena
coordinate system.

## Hypothesis

If the flat dense triplet model struggles because cross-mouse keypoint edges add
noise, this variant should improve pose, structure, and ordering metrics while
possibly weakening social-interaction trajectory cues. Compare the result
against the flat dense triplet and flat dense single-mouse runs.

## Inspect configuration

```sh {"id":"01M25WITHINMOUSE5FPSCONFIG","interpreter":"/home/splion/Desktop/personal/interpreting-social-navigation/.venv/bin/python3.13"}
